{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.PlancherelTiltDerivative","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PlancherelTiltDerivative","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TiltDerivativeCovariance","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIPlancherelConditional"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.plancherel_tiltNum_eval_one_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.plancherel_tiltNum_eval_one_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PlancherelTiltDerivative.lean#L101-L109","doc":"The tilted mean **vanishes at `x = 1`** — the obstruction, stated for the real objects.\n\nThis is why evaluating on the limit shape proves nothing: the quantity being computed is\nidentically zero at the point where such an evaluation happens. The content of the\nreformulation is that the *derivative* there is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.plancherel_tilt_deriv_eq_wCov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.plancherel_tilt_deriv_eq_wCov","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PlancherelTiltDerivative.lean#L87-L99","doc":"**`M₁` IS the tilt derivative, at the actual Plancherel measure.**\n\nFor *any* integer statistic `hgt` used as the tilt exponent, the derivative at `x = 1` of\nthe `hgt`-tilted Plancherel mean of `ω₃` equals the Plancherel covariance of `hgt` with\n`ω₃`. Taking `hgt = Σ□h` gives `M₁`.\n\nConditional on `[PlancherelSnData n]` — see the epistemic-status note in the module\ndocstring. Says nothing about the sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.plancherel_wMean_omega3_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.plancherel_wMean_omega3_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PlancherelTiltDerivative.lean#L82-L85","doc":"The Plancherel weighted mean of `ω₃` is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.plancherel_weighted_omega3_sum_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.plancherel_weighted_omega3_sum_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PlancherelTiltDerivative.lean#L64-L80","doc":"**The Plancherel `ω₃`-mean vanishes — derived, not assumed.**\n\n`∑_λ dim(λ)² · ω₃(λ) = 0`, exactly, from the two `PlancherelSnData` fields. This is the\nhypothesis of `tilt_deriv_eq_wCov`, and it is the same fact that makes a limit-shape\nevaluation of `M₁` return `0 ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.omega3Q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.omega3Q","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PlancherelTiltDerivative.lean#L57-L62","doc":"`ω₃(λ) = Σ_c c(c)² − binom(n,2)`, the centred content-square statistic, as a rational.\n\nKept over `ℚ` rather than `ℤ` because `binom(n,2) = n(n−1)/2` is not an integer-valued\nexpression in this spelling, and because the tilt identity divides. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.plancherelWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.plancherelWeight","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PlancherelTiltDerivative.lean#L54-L55","doc":"The Plancherel weight `w λ = dim(λ)²`, as a rational. ","signatureChunk":0}]}